v1.15.0
docker-publish: verify the image's entrypoint binary resolves its shared libraries (incl. glibc symbol versions) against the runtime base, and that it starts without a crash signature, before pushing. Warn-only by default; set CI_LINKAGE_CHECK=enforce|off

Previously:
- INFRA-1076 make CI bot-tolerant: attribute a fleet-merge deploy (detected by the clever-fleet[bot] co-author trailer) to the fleet bot, and skip the CI-failure notify for bot authors instead of failing the job
- Make the shared pr-review skill the only review path, dropping the inline prompt and @claude-beta gate
- Error when apps share a Dockerfile path but publish different artifacts
- Route @claude-beta reviews through the shared pr-review skill
- Support repos with no launch.yaml
- Move k8s deploys to platform events
